{#-
  BLOCK: bands — §06's `bands`. The price-distribution bar chart.

  Moved verbatim from the chart section of `_build_analytics_body`. Each row is
  a two-cell table: the filled bar and the remainder, which is how a bar chart
  is drawn in an email — no CSS width animation, no SVG, no background-image,
  because Outlook supports none of them and Gmail strips the rest.

  B6 IS WHY THE WIDTHS ARE COMPUTED IN PYTHON. The register records bars
  normalised to the largest band while the labels showed share of total, so
  Move-Up read 43% beside a bar filled to 100%. `bar_pct` and the percentage
  label have to come from the same place or they drift again; they are computed
  together in `_band_rows()` and arrive here already reconciled.
-#}
              <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
                {% for b in bands %}
                      <tr>
                        <td style="padding: 8px 0;">
                          <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%">
                            <tr>
                              <td width="110" style="vertical-align: middle; padding-right: 12px;">
                                <p style="margin: 0; {{ b.label_style }}">{{ b.label }}</p>
                                <p style="margin: 2px 0 0; font-size: 11px; color: #6b7280;">{{ b.count }} listings</p>
                              </td>
                              <td style="vertical-align: middle;">
                                <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;">
                                  <tr>
                                    <td width="{{ b.bar_pct }}%" style="height: 24px; background-color: {{ b.bar_bg }};"></td>
                                    <td width="{{ b.empty_pct }}%" style="height: 24px; background-color: #e5e7eb;"></td>
                                  </tr>
                                </table>
                              </td>
                              <td width="50" align="right" style="vertical-align: middle; padding-left: 10px;">
                                <span style="{{ b.pct_style }}">{{ b.pct }}</span>
                              </td>
                            </tr>
                          </table>
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                {%- endfor %}
              </table>
